coder › All 7 tests pass. Here's what I changed.

**`src/range.ts`** — rewrote `overlaps` with two helpers:
- `endpoint(value)` parses each endpoint and throws `TypeError: not a valid date: <value>` when `Date.parse` returns `NaN` (instead of the old silent `false`).
- `parse(range)` parses both endpoints and throws `RangeError` if the end is before the start.
- `overlaps` now uses strict `<` on both sides, so touching ranges (one's end equal to the other's start) don't overlap, while same-start ranges do, and a zero-length range overlaps nothing — including itself, since `start === end` fails the `<` test.

**`src/range.test.ts`** — added six tests covering: touching ranges don't overlap, same-start ranges do overlap, zero-length range overlaps nothing (including itself), unparseable start throws `TypeError` naming the value, unparseable end throws `TypeError` naming it, and end-before-start throws `RangeError`.

One note: I dropped the `aStart <= bEnd`/`bStart <= aEnd` inclusive comparisons in favor of strict `<`, which is the core fix — the end being exclusive means equality on the touching side is no longer overlap.
